      "S5"
    ],
    "word_count": 95,
    "html": "<p>For Keke Rosberg, earning a living in racing involved selling as well as driving. He offered sponsors space on his suit or car and promoted their products. Commercial income supplemented his race earnings, helping sustain a career that took him between championships on different continents.</p>\r\n<p>Rosberg saw another commercial opening in racing engineers' knowledge. His idea for Team Rosberg Engineering was to apply experience in chassis development and tuning to production vehicles. The business grew into a development partner for car manufacturers, bringing methods learned in competition into the design and testing of road cars.</p>\r\n"
  },
